4 CONC gt;, &lt;a&gt;James Wesley Amburn Jr&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a&gt;Gladolia Virginia Amburn&lt;/a&gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Additional information: &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;LifeSketch: Bio: Lilly A. 
4 CONC (Amburn) Rose Lilly A. (Amburn) Rose, 78, of Swansea Mall Drive passed away Thursday, November 24, 2005 at Charlton Memorial Hospital in Fall River. She was the wife of the late Willard H. Rose. Born 
4 CONC in Blair, West Virginia on January 7, 1927 the daughter of the late James and Dovie (Tabor) Amburn. She worked as a supervisor for Raytheon for twenty- five years before retiring in thirteen years ago
4 CONC . She was a member of the Bethany Grace Gospel Church in Swansea. Mrs. Rose was very Active in the church she also was a Sunday school teacher. She enjoyed watching the Red Sox, Fishing, Boating, and 
4 CONC camping. Survivors are six daughters Linda Powell of Bedford, Texas Sharon Silvia of Swansea, MA Gloria Thompson of Raleigh, NC Rebecca Adler of Suffern, NY Janelle Hart of Exeter, RI Tracey Boehm of 
4 CONC Johnston, RI two sons Robert Rose of New Prot Richey, Florida Daniel Rose of Raynham, MA nineteen grandchildren and eleven great grandchildren, and many nieces and nephews. Funeral Information:Her fun
4 CONC eral will be held on Wednesday, November 30, 2005 at 10 am in the Hathaway Community Home for Funerals, 900 Buffinton St., Somerset, MA. Relatives and friends are invited to attend, burial to follow i
4 CONC n Mount Hope Cemetery Swansea. Calling hours are Tuesday, November 29, 2005 from 4-7 pm.
